# /sdd-sync

Purpose:
  Propose and execute sync operations for detected drift.

Owns: commands/sdd-sync.sdd

Description:
  Reads drift reports from /sdd-drift, proposes SYNC_CODE / SYNC_SDD /
  SYNC_BOTH operations, and executes them with human approval at
  READ_WRITE gates.

Usage:
  /sdd-sync
  /sdd-sync --drift <D<id>>
  /sdd-sync --auto-approve <low-risk-only>
  /sdd-sync --dry-run

Options:
  --drift        Sync specific drift record
  --auto-approve Auto-approve LOW confidence, NO_CHANGE ops
  --dry-run      Show plan without executing

Mode: READ_WRITE

Rules:
  [SYN-01] /sdd-sync MUST require human approval for HIGH severity syncs.
  [SYN-02] /sdd-sync MUST produce @decision.* for every SYNC_SDD operation.
  [SYN-03] /sdd-sync MUST produce @task.* for every SYNC_CODE operation.
  [SYN-04] /sdd-sync MUST produce @task.* for every SYNC_BOTH operation.
  [SYN-05] /sdd-sync MUST NOT execute NO_CHANGE without explicit --force.

Navigation:
  INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
  DriftSpec: @../lifecycle/drift.sdd
  Queries: @../queries/sync-operations.sdd
  Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd
  Tasks: @../tasks/TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd

State: +
